{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And they shall take some of the blood.</b> This is the receiving of the blood. One might say, in the hand? Scripture says: <b>which is in the basin</b> (Mekhilta)." "<b>The doorposts.</b> They are the uprights — one on this side of the entrance and one on that side." "<b>The lintel.</b> The upper one, upon which the door leans (shoqef) when they close it — לינטי״ל בְּלַעַז. And the term שְׁקִיפָה means a blow, as in ״קוֹל עָלֶה נִדָּף״ (Leviticus 26) — דְשָׁקִיף, a wound (חַבּוּרָה) — מַשְׁקוֹפֵי." "<b>On the houses in which they shall eat it.</b> And not on the lintel and doorposts of a straw-house or a cattle-house, where one does not dwell within them (cf. Mekhilta)."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {2 "Rashi reads נִדָּף as from the root שׁקף, citing the Targum's rendering דְשָׁקִיף and glossing it as חַבּוּרָה, 'a wound/blow'; the la'az is Old French lintel."}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:51:34.059348203Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}